+# The Network workbench
+
+<!-- impeccable:product-schema 1 -->
+
+## Platform
+
+web
+
+## Users
+
+Members manage the facts, preferences and private invitations used to find useful connections. Operators review proposals, inspect outcomes and handle safety cases. This local workbench lets Nubs review the full MVP without access to Shaw's private repository.
+
+## Product Purpose
+
+Help members find worthwhile experiences and connections with less coordination effort, while retaining independent consent and privacy controls.
+
+## Operating Context
+
+Confirmed source: the current Network PRD sections 28-38. This build uses synthetic local fixture identities and local data. Server-issued sessions determine authority. A local operation never represents a real message or real encounter.
+
+## Capabilities and Constraints
+
+Render authoritative API DTOs and supplied action descriptors. Include all seventeen admin modules in PRD 35.2. Keep drafts, pending actions, completed actions and failures distinct. Do not infer privileged access from client fields. Do not expose private decline details to another member. No live contacts, publication, payments or external provider effects are authorized.
+
+## Brand Commitments
+
+Extend Eliza's neutral UI and orange action accent. Use existing React UI primitives where available.
+
+## Accessibility and Inclusion
+
+Support keyboard navigation, clear form labels, readable contrast, visible errors, small-screen use and assistive technologies.
