@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Network member runtime capability
+
+Hosts explicitly provide an authenticated member/room port. The plugin reads that member's authorized context and executes domain commands through the port. It owns no membership, graph, queue, scheduling or transport storage. Staff commands and identity verification are never model-facing.
+
+The closed local workbench composes the genuine Shared Eliza runtime with a labelled deterministic model. Its fixture grammar covers private facet proposals/readback, asks, participation changes, opportunity responses, relay and scheduling. Complete private history and native trajectories use the canonical owners. Contact grants, age, profile confirmation/sharing, proactive and romance opt-in remain explicit member controls.
+
+Local pasted sources accept labelled facets and preserve previous member choices. Profiling questions and authored-source recommendations use the native approval queue, explicit staff review, existing Clock, Domain budgets and unanswered policy, and the shared closed mock delivery implementation. No source fetch, paid inference or real sender is enabled.
+
+Run its tests using the repository source-alias Vitest configuration. Shared Cloud runtime composition loads it only when the trusted host supplies the port.
